1
00:00:01,735 --> 00:00:03,294
<i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:04,770
General Wade's
landing craft docked.

3
00:00:05,038 --> 00:00:06,472
<i>His convoy's on
the way here now.</i>

4
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:08,509
<i>Reunification day is today.</i>

5
00:00:08,575 --> 00:00:11,135
- Captain Gordon.
- General, welcome to Gotham.

6
00:00:11,211 --> 00:00:12,211
Incoming!

7
00:00:12,279 --> 00:00:14,009
Get back!

8
00:00:14,648 --> 00:00:18,016
(filtered breathing)

9
00:00:23,724 --> 00:00:26,159
Eduardo. What did
Walker do to you?

10
00:00:26,226 --> 00:00:27,421
Eduardo's dead, Jim.

11
00:00:27,494 --> 00:00:28,757
There is only Bane now.

12
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:32,727
Everything I have done here
is about punishing Gotham

13
00:00:32,799 --> 00:00:35,291
for the sins of Bruce Wayne.

14
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:36,530
I'm not leaving.

15
00:00:36,603 --> 00:00:38,037
And I don't think I can

16
00:00:38,105 --> 00:00:40,165
let you leave... either.

17
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:41,333
What are you doing?

18
00:00:41,408 --> 00:00:42,808
(grunting)

19
00:00:44,211 --> 00:00:45,736
Ra's al Ghul.

20
00:00:45,812 --> 00:00:46,609
This is revenge

21
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:47,704
for his death.

22
00:00:47,781 --> 00:00:48,781
And who am I?

23
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:50,073
You're his daughter.

24
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:51,743
(grunting)

25
00:00:51,818 --> 00:00:54,083
(shouting)

26
00:00:55,155 --> 00:00:56,384
Barbara Kean.

27
00:00:56,456 --> 00:00:57,685
Run!

28
00:00:57,758 --> 00:01:00,091
My name is Nyssa al Ghul.

29
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:02,061
I believe you knew my father.

30
00:01:02,129 --> 00:01:03,369
- Where's Nyssa?
- I don't know,

31
00:01:03,397 --> 00:01:04,407
but she's planning
on using the military

32
00:01:04,431 --> 00:01:05,364
to wipe out Gotham.

33
00:01:05,432 --> 00:01:06,764
I can order them to stand down.

34
00:01:06,833 --> 00:01:08,073
Then let's get you out of here.

35
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:11,365
This is General Wade.

36
00:01:11,438 --> 00:01:12,565
Begin your bombing run

37
00:01:12,639 --> 00:01:13,719
- on my order.
- Wait, wait.

38
00:01:17,578 --> 00:01:20,446
(explosions in distance)

39
00:01:21,515 --> 00:01:23,450
(helicopter blades whirring)

40
00:01:23,517 --> 00:01:25,452
(indistinct chatter)

41
00:01:38,565 --> 00:01:40,693
GORDON: We need
to get ahold of Barbara.

42
00:01:40,767 --> 00:01:42,395
Nyssa al Ghul's coming for her.

43
00:01:42,469 --> 00:01:44,847
The sooner she and Lee get
back here with the baby, the better.

44
00:01:44,871 --> 00:01:46,549
LUCIUS: We got refugees
coming in from all over Gotham, Jim.

45
00:01:46,573 --> 00:01:47,597
People are scared.

46
00:01:47,674 --> 00:01:49,267
I know you're not one to quit,

47
00:01:49,343 --> 00:01:51,154
but if there was ever a
time to wave the white flag,

48
00:01:51,178 --> 00:01:52,178
now is it.

49
00:01:52,245 --> 00:01:55,238
Nyssa al Ghul doesn't want
to just conquer Gotham...

50
00:01:55,315 --> 00:01:56,681
She wants to destroy it,

51
00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:58,378
kill everyone she finds.

52
00:01:58,452 --> 00:02:01,388
The only thing standing between
her and these people is us.

53
00:02:01,455 --> 00:02:03,117
Gather the team.

54
00:02:03,190 --> 00:02:04,658
Get every able-bodied refugee

55
00:02:04,725 --> 00:02:07,456
down into the bunkers
beneath the GCPD.

56
00:02:07,527 --> 00:02:09,792
Why do I get the
feeling he's concocting

57
00:02:09,863 --> 00:02:12,332
an elaborate plan
to get us all killed?

58
00:02:12,399 --> 00:02:15,301
Better gather up these refugees.

59
00:02:18,905 --> 00:02:21,841
Look at him.

60
00:02:21,908 --> 00:02:25,208
The medics did everything
they could to stabilize him.

61
00:02:26,513 --> 00:02:29,608
Now all we can do is wait.

62
00:02:30,684 --> 00:02:32,915
This is my fault.

63
00:02:35,889 --> 00:02:38,449
I sent him on this mission.

64
00:02:38,525 --> 00:02:41,324
Alfred knew what he
was signing up for, Bruce.

65
00:02:41,395 --> 00:02:43,364
We all did.

66
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:46,628
Nyssa and Bane are
coming after me and Barbara.

67
00:02:47,334 --> 00:02:49,360
Coming after Gotham.

68
00:02:49,803 --> 00:02:53,365
Because of what we did to Ra's.

69
00:02:54,341 --> 00:02:56,776
What you did was stop him.

70
00:02:57,911 --> 00:02:59,470
Twice.

71
00:02:59,946 --> 00:03:03,178
We'll stop his psycho
daughter together.

72
00:03:10,924 --> 00:03:13,894
I'm sure you
recognize this knife.

73
00:03:15,495 --> 00:03:16,758
You touch my baby,

74
00:03:16,830 --> 00:03:18,423
and I will turn you
into a pile of ash,

75
00:03:18,498 --> 00:03:20,296
just like I did your father.

76
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:23,735
A bit cruel, don't you think?

77
00:03:23,804 --> 00:03:25,966
To let this little
one get too attached

78
00:03:26,239 --> 00:03:27,571
when you won't be around

79
00:03:27,641 --> 00:03:28,700
much longer.

80
00:03:28,775 --> 00:03:30,209
(shudders) Mmm.

81
00:03:30,277 --> 00:03:31,802
(cooing)

82
00:03:31,878 --> 00:03:34,347
Soon, you and Bruce Wayne

83
00:03:34,414 --> 00:03:36,212
will see Gotham

84
00:03:36,283 --> 00:03:40,448
and Jim Gordon's precious
Green Zone destroyed.

85
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:43,721
Then I'll allow you to die.

86
00:03:43,790 --> 00:03:47,659
My father made his
name destroying empires.

87
00:03:47,728 --> 00:03:50,562
Now it's my turn.

88
00:03:53,633 --> 00:03:55,329
(panting) Hello.

89
00:03:55,402 --> 00:03:57,530
Listen to me. There
is a submarine

90
00:03:57,604 --> 00:03:59,402
in the docks, full
of Gotham's gold.

91
00:03:59,473 --> 00:04:00,532
It's yours.

92
00:04:00,607 --> 00:04:02,633
Just leave the city.

93
00:04:02,709 --> 00:04:04,371
Let me and my baby go.

94
00:04:04,444 --> 00:04:07,471
(cooing) No.

95
00:04:07,547 --> 00:04:11,006
I think I'll keep
this little one

96
00:04:11,284 --> 00:04:14,277
and raise her as my own.

97
00:04:15,856 --> 00:04:17,324
As an al Ghul.

98
00:04:17,390 --> 00:04:18,790
(laughing)

99
00:04:21,995 --> 00:04:23,930
I take it the army has landed.

100
00:04:23,997 --> 00:04:25,795
They're just awaiting my orders.

101
00:04:25,866 --> 00:04:27,858
Then what are you waiting for?

102
00:04:31,638 --> 00:04:35,336
What a cute little baby.

103
00:04:36,443 --> 00:04:38,378
(indistinct chatter)

104
00:04:49,422 --> 00:04:50,481
Wait, what?

105
00:04:50,557 --> 00:04:52,492
You're ordering us to
destroy the Green Zone?

106
00:04:52,559 --> 00:04:55,324
Anyone still in Gotham
is an enemy of the state.

107
00:04:55,395 --> 00:04:57,473
I won't be party to the
murder of civilians, General.

108
00:04:57,497 --> 00:05:00,057
Then you're relieved of command.

109
00:05:00,333 --> 00:05:01,926
The hell are you?

110
00:05:02,002 --> 00:05:03,061
(filtered breathing)

111
00:05:03,336 --> 00:05:04,634
I'm your new commander.

112
00:05:04,704 --> 00:05:06,900
(snap)

113
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:10,774
Does anybody else have a
problem with the general's orders?

114
00:05:11,845 --> 00:05:12,938
Good.

115
00:05:13,013 --> 00:05:15,448
Let's get started.

116
00:05:15,515 --> 00:05:17,780
♪♪♪♪

117
00:05:29,496 --> 00:05:30,964
What's the matter?

118
00:05:31,031 --> 00:05:34,968
Can we really be so cavalier
about the destruction of Gotham?

119
00:05:35,035 --> 00:05:37,595
(sighs) Let me think about that.

120
00:05:37,671 --> 00:05:38,570
Yes!

121
00:05:38,638 --> 00:05:40,470
(groans)

122
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:41,701
Damn it!

123
00:05:41,775 --> 00:05:43,710
Oswald!

124
00:05:43,777 --> 00:05:44,904
Where are you going?

125
00:05:44,978 --> 00:05:46,640
Oswald!

126
00:05:46,713 --> 00:05:48,807
This is my city,
and I will be damned

127
00:05:48,882 --> 00:05:50,783
if I'm gonna let
those bastards take it!

128
00:05:50,851 --> 00:05:52,376
I cannot let you do this.

129
00:05:52,452 --> 00:05:53,715
You, of all people,

130
00:05:53,787 --> 00:05:56,347
should want to
stop those monsters.

131
00:05:56,423 --> 00:05:58,824
They forced you
to destroy Haven,

132
00:05:58,892 --> 00:06:00,827
to murder hundreds
of innocent civilians.

133
00:06:00,894 --> 00:06:02,920
You're just gonna let
'em get away with it?

134
00:06:02,996 --> 00:06:04,658
I was kind of
planning on it, yeah.

135
00:06:05,398 --> 00:06:06,798
Very well.

136
00:06:06,867 --> 00:06:08,995
I'm going to follow my heart.

137
00:06:09,736 --> 00:06:10,863
Oswald!

138
00:06:12,706 --> 00:06:14,436
You have been
down this road before.

139
00:06:15,408 --> 00:06:18,401
Following your heart has
never worked out for you.

140
00:06:20,714 --> 00:06:22,114
Perhaps.

141
00:06:22,382 --> 00:06:23,822
But perhaps you
could learn something

142
00:06:23,884 --> 00:06:25,978
if you listened to <i>this</i>

143
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:27,884
instead of <i>this.</i>

144
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:31,824
I'm gonna miss you,

145
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:34,157
Edward. (crying)

146
00:06:34,427 --> 00:06:35,895
I'll miss you, too, Oswald.

147
00:06:37,030 --> 00:06:39,693
I'm not talking to you.

148
00:06:39,766 --> 00:06:40,961
I'm talking to the...

149
00:06:41,034 --> 00:06:42,525
God!

150
00:06:42,602 --> 00:06:44,594
(chuckles) Come on, baby.

151
00:06:44,671 --> 00:06:46,401
All right.

152
00:06:46,473 --> 00:06:47,497
Okay.

153
00:06:47,574 --> 00:06:48,803
Good boy.

154
00:06:52,512 --> 00:06:54,777
(panting)

155
00:06:54,848 --> 00:06:56,441
Go with the man in green.

156
00:06:56,516 --> 00:06:57,677
(shuddering inhale)

157
00:06:57,751 --> 00:06:59,652
You'll be safe.

158
00:06:59,719 --> 00:07:02,712
Oswald, if you
walk off this dock,

159
00:07:02,789 --> 00:07:04,621
I'm taking this submarine.
(sniffles, exhales)

160
00:07:04,691 --> 00:07:06,626
And the treasure!

161
00:07:06,693 --> 00:07:08,628
Nyssa al Ghul wants to
kill everyone in Gotham.

162
00:07:08,695 --> 00:07:12,427
But, to get to us, the army has
to follow the Western Corridor.

163
00:07:12,499 --> 00:07:13,659
That's where we make a stand.

164
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:14,700
We got a handful of men.

165
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:16,669
How are we gonna
take on an army?

166
00:07:16,736 --> 00:07:18,728
We just have to slow the
army down long enough

167
00:07:18,805 --> 00:07:21,001
to get General Wade out
from under Nyssa's control.

168
00:07:21,074 --> 00:07:22,838
Then he can reverse
the invasion order.

169
00:07:23,476 --> 00:07:25,104
We're trying to
reach the Sirens.

170
00:07:25,178 --> 00:07:26,077
Still no luck.

171
00:07:26,146 --> 00:07:28,081
All right. I'll go.

172
00:07:28,148 --> 00:07:29,616
Jim.

173
00:07:29,683 --> 00:07:30,860
I need to get Barbara
and Lee back here.

174
00:07:30,884 --> 00:07:32,995
I'll meet you at the barricades.
I know you haven't seen

175
00:07:33,019 --> 00:07:35,614
your kid yet, but the
GCPD needs a leader,

176
00:07:35,689 --> 00:07:37,089
and they're looking to you.

177
00:07:37,157 --> 00:07:38,216
I'll go to Sirens.

178
00:07:38,491 --> 00:07:39,982
Okay.

179
00:07:42,095 --> 00:07:44,530
(siren wailing in distance)

180
00:07:47,167 --> 00:07:49,602
You sure you want to do this?

181
00:07:49,669 --> 00:07:52,036
It doesn't take two of us
to track the general's signal.

182
00:07:52,105 --> 00:07:54,574
And if Jim's making a stand,
that's where I should be.

183
00:07:54,641 --> 00:07:55,836
Okay.

184
00:07:55,909 --> 00:07:57,935
Wayne Enterprises EMP,

185
00:07:58,011 --> 00:08:00,742
smoke bombs, signal jammers.

186
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:02,908
Not enough to
even the odds, but...

187
00:08:02,983 --> 00:08:04,246
it may buy you some time.

188
00:08:04,517 --> 00:08:06,008
What's this?

189
00:08:06,086 --> 00:08:09,488
Ah. Remember the
Nightwing Project?

190
00:08:09,556 --> 00:08:12,025
Portable, next-gen stealth tech.

191
00:08:12,092 --> 00:08:14,926
Put it on any aircraft,
and it's invisible to radar.

192
00:08:14,995 --> 00:08:17,115
But, unfortunately, it also
seems to serve as a beacon

193
00:08:17,163 --> 00:08:19,189
to certain animals.

194
00:08:19,265 --> 00:08:20,563
Never know.

195
00:08:20,633 --> 00:08:21,633
Might find a use for it.

196
00:08:27,607 --> 00:08:29,075
Oswald, come in.

197
00:08:29,142 --> 00:08:30,906
(chuckles)

198
00:08:30,977 --> 00:08:33,811
Still have those eyes in
the back of your head, Jim.

199
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:35,610
No. (sighs)

200
00:08:35,682 --> 00:08:38,880
You just have a remarkably
recognizable odor.

201
00:08:38,952 --> 00:08:41,683
Part dandy, part snake.

202
00:08:41,755 --> 00:08:43,815
After all these years,
it hasn't changed.

203
00:08:43,890 --> 00:08:44,890
Drink?

204
00:08:44,958 --> 00:08:46,824
No, thank you.

205
00:08:46,893 --> 00:08:49,021
Dulls the senses.

206
00:08:49,095 --> 00:08:50,620
That's what I was going for.

207
00:08:52,298 --> 00:08:54,130
Surprised you're still here.

208
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:56,226
Figured you'd be
long gone by now.

209
00:08:56,302 --> 00:09:00,262
That storm you've warned
me about for so long,

210
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,600
it's finally here.

211
00:09:05,078 --> 00:09:08,879
We've shared some
turbulent times, you and I.

212
00:09:08,948 --> 00:09:10,883
That we have.

213
00:09:10,950 --> 00:09:13,249
When you spared my
life on the pier that day,

214
00:09:13,319 --> 00:09:15,914
banished me from Gotham,

215
00:09:15,989 --> 00:09:18,549
that was the most
lost I've ever been.

216
00:09:18,625 --> 00:09:19,923
(chuckles)

217
00:09:19,993 --> 00:09:22,326
Because I was away
from the city, you see.

218
00:09:22,595 --> 00:09:23,619
(chuckles)

219
00:09:24,631 --> 00:09:27,100
It's part of me.

220
00:09:27,167 --> 00:09:28,897
You know what I'm talking about,

221
00:09:28,968 --> 00:09:30,698
because it's part of you, too.

222
00:09:30,770 --> 00:09:32,238
(chuckles)

223
00:09:32,305 --> 00:09:33,898
Sure, I could escape...

224
00:09:33,973 --> 00:09:35,032
With money, I might add...

225
00:09:35,108 --> 00:09:37,043
But then what?

226
00:09:37,110 --> 00:09:38,772
Stand on the shores
of the mainland

227
00:09:38,845 --> 00:09:41,246
and watch the army
burn it to the ground?

228
00:09:41,314 --> 00:09:43,977
Then watch
tasteless industrialists

229
00:09:44,050 --> 00:09:46,849
and vapid
politicians rebuild it?

230
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:47,920
(chuckles)

231
00:09:47,987 --> 00:09:49,717
No.

232
00:09:50,223 --> 00:09:53,159
My life is etched on
the walls of every alley

233
00:09:53,226 --> 00:09:55,320
and dirty warehouse here.

234
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:59,965
My blood lives in
its broken concrete.

235
00:10:02,802 --> 00:10:04,270
I'm staying to fight.

236
00:10:05,138 --> 00:10:06,800
For my legacy.

237
00:10:06,873 --> 00:10:08,034
BULLOCK: Hey.

238
00:10:09,042 --> 00:10:10,920
The army just busted
through the GCPD checkpoint.

239
00:10:10,944 --> 00:10:12,879
They're heading
to the barricades.

240
00:10:12,946 --> 00:10:14,141
Bane's leading them.

241
00:10:14,214 --> 00:10:15,238
How many men?

242
00:10:15,315 --> 00:10:17,011
(sighs) 600, 700?

243
00:10:17,083 --> 00:10:19,177
- Still want to fight?
- (gulps)

244
00:10:19,252 --> 00:10:20,811
How many do we have?

245
00:10:20,887 --> 00:10:21,752
Maybe 30?

246
00:10:21,821 --> 00:10:22,686
(laughs)

247
00:10:22,755 --> 00:10:24,223
Thirty-one.

248
00:10:26,025 --> 00:10:27,825
Takes two men to pilot
that submarine, Oswald.

249
00:10:27,861 --> 00:10:28,861
The dog can't do it.

250
00:10:28,928 --> 00:10:30,055
(exhales)

251
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:32,759
Ditto on that blood
and concrete thing.

252
00:10:32,832 --> 00:10:35,768
Kind of like this
city the way it is.

253
00:10:35,835 --> 00:10:37,394
Shall we?

254
00:10:37,670 --> 00:10:39,229
I believe time is
of the essence.

255
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:41,035
Gentlemen.

256
00:10:41,107 --> 00:10:43,975
Remind me to talk to
you about that full pardon.

257
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:48,945
♪♪♪♪

258
00:11:12,238 --> 00:11:14,002
Alvarez!

259
00:11:14,073 --> 00:11:15,803
Harper, Bruce!

260
00:11:15,875 --> 00:11:17,434
You take the left flank.

261
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:19,201
Harvey and I
will take the right.

262
00:11:19,279 --> 00:11:21,680
Holy Mary, Mother and Joseph.

263
00:11:25,952 --> 00:11:28,046
BANE: Captain Gordon...

264
00:11:28,121 --> 00:11:30,750
I always knew you
had a savior complex,

265
00:11:30,823 --> 00:11:32,382
but this is too much.

266
00:11:32,458 --> 00:11:34,859
What happened to you, Eduardo?

267
00:11:34,928 --> 00:11:36,438
There was a time when
you would have been up

268
00:11:36,462 --> 00:11:38,055
on these barricades with me.

269
00:11:38,131 --> 00:11:43,035
Yes... but that was before
I found my true purpose.

270
00:11:43,102 --> 00:11:45,401
Stand by.

271
00:11:45,471 --> 00:11:48,134
Fire on my command.

272
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:50,302
Jim, it's a lot of
innocent soldiers

273
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:52,140
down there just
following orders.

274
00:11:53,246 --> 00:11:55,806
Target Bane and
Nyssa's commandos.

275
00:11:55,882 --> 00:11:56,906
Fire on my command.

276
00:11:58,218 --> 00:11:59,709
For Gotham.

277
00:12:11,998 --> 00:12:14,024
(groans)

278
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,035
SELINA: Lee?

279
00:12:16,102 --> 00:12:17,764
(gunfire in distance)

280
00:12:17,837 --> 00:12:19,032
Selina.

281
00:12:19,105 --> 00:12:21,870
Hey. Come on, we
got to get out of here.

282
00:12:21,941 --> 00:12:24,308
Where's Barbara and the baby?

283
00:12:24,377 --> 00:12:26,437
(exhales) Nyssa
al Ghul took them.

284
00:12:26,512 --> 00:12:27,878
We have to tell Jim.

285
00:12:27,947 --> 00:12:29,108
Yeah.

286
00:12:29,182 --> 00:12:31,117
(gunfire continues)

287
00:12:33,886 --> 00:12:36,321
The Narrows.

288
00:12:41,961 --> 00:12:43,486
They never stood a chance.

289
00:12:44,430 --> 00:12:47,298
The ones who could
escaped to the GCPD.

290
00:12:47,367 --> 00:12:49,802
Then that's where I'm needed.

291
00:12:54,507 --> 00:12:56,066
(grunts)

292
00:13:02,181 --> 00:13:03,809
(grenade whistling)

293
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:08,220
- Target Jim Gordon.
- (grunts)

294
00:13:08,288 --> 00:13:10,223
I'm sorry! I don't
think he can hear you

295
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:11,986
through the bullet in his ear!

296
00:13:12,058 --> 00:13:13,424
(groans)

297
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:18,821
Eddie!

298
00:13:19,832 --> 00:13:22,324
(screaming)

299
00:13:24,404 --> 00:13:26,532
They're only
delaying the inevitable.

300
00:13:28,107 --> 00:13:30,303
Jim, that thing's
pointing right at us!

301
00:13:33,913 --> 00:13:35,313
(groans)

302
00:13:35,381 --> 00:13:37,009
BANE: Go, go, go, go, go!

303
00:13:41,854 --> 00:13:44,949
Find me Jim Gordon
and Bruce Wayne.

304
00:13:45,992 --> 00:13:47,269
If the army gets
through the barricades,

305
00:13:47,293 --> 00:13:49,438
they'll have a straight shot to
the GCPD and the people there.

306
00:13:49,462 --> 00:13:51,556
We need to find another
way to slow them down.

307
00:13:51,831 --> 00:13:53,322
I think I have a way.

308
00:13:55,468 --> 00:13:56,979
GORDON: Gather all
the ammunition you can.

309
00:13:57,003 --> 00:13:58,938
Fall back to the GCPD.

310
00:13:59,005 --> 00:14:00,303
Go, go now!

311
00:14:00,373 --> 00:14:01,466
Fall back!

312
00:14:01,541 --> 00:14:03,373
We got to go. (grunts)

313
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:16,348
Well, that was a disaster.

314
00:14:16,422 --> 00:14:18,550
Come on, Oswald, we
have to keep moving.

315
00:14:18,624 --> 00:14:21,594
Where? There's
nowhere to hide, Jim.

316
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:24,922
Wherever we go,
the army will find us.

317
00:14:24,997 --> 00:14:26,041
<i>LUCIUS (over radio):
Get me Gordon.</i>

318
00:14:26,065 --> 00:14:27,431
It's Lucius.

319
00:14:28,401 --> 00:14:30,412
Tell me you were able to
track the general's signal.

320
00:14:30,436 --> 00:14:32,564
It's coming from City
Hall, but there's a problem.

321
00:14:32,638 --> 00:14:34,266
Selina radioed.

322
00:14:34,340 --> 00:14:38,038
<i>Barbara and the baby were
kidnapped by Nyssa al Ghul.</i>

323
00:14:38,111 --> 00:14:39,579
General Wade's at City Hall.

324
00:14:39,645 --> 00:14:42,137
Chances are Nyssa,
Barbara and the baby are, too.

325
00:14:42,215 --> 00:14:44,616
Our best bet is for me to
sneak into City Hall alone.

326
00:14:44,884 --> 00:14:47,353
One good electrical zap should
short out the general's chip,

327
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:49,420
then you can get him to
reverse the invasion order.

328
00:14:50,156 --> 00:14:52,182
See you back at the GCPD.

329
00:14:52,258 --> 00:14:54,557
Get Barbara and
the baby back safe.

330
00:14:54,627 --> 00:14:56,562
Come on. Hey, move!

331
00:14:57,363 --> 00:14:59,332
Upsy-daisy, Oswald.
(Oswald grunting)

332
00:14:59,399 --> 00:15:00,958
We're running out of time.

333
00:15:01,033 --> 00:15:04,401
(gasps) Just give me one minute.

334
00:15:04,470 --> 00:15:06,996
I'm so sorry.

335
00:15:07,073 --> 00:15:09,633
I saw the grenade
and I froze. (exhales)

336
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:11,343
I'm sor... Shh.

337
00:15:12,412 --> 00:15:15,007
It's the least I could do.

338
00:15:16,949 --> 00:15:17,949
But tell me...

339
00:15:20,119 --> 00:15:22,350
Does it look bad?

340
00:15:24,524 --> 00:15:26,493
No, it's just a scr... (gags)

341
00:15:26,559 --> 00:15:28,425
Looks fine. Let's go.

342
00:15:28,494 --> 00:15:31,328
Where'd everybody go?

343
00:15:31,397 --> 00:15:33,491
She's gonna need some morphine.

344
00:15:33,566 --> 00:15:34,566
(explosion)

345
00:15:34,634 --> 00:15:37,934
And this bandage needs changing.

346
00:15:38,004 --> 00:15:39,700
Lee.

347
00:15:39,972 --> 00:15:40,996
Bruce. Is Jim...?

348
00:15:41,073 --> 00:15:42,974
He's okay. For now.

349
00:15:43,042 --> 00:15:45,202
We'll need to get Jeremiah's
battery from the basement.

350
00:15:46,279 --> 00:15:48,305
After the bridges went
down, Lucius re-modified

351
00:15:48,381 --> 00:15:51,215
Jeremiah's bomb to be
used for its original purpose...

352
00:15:51,984 --> 00:15:53,247
as a battery.

353
00:15:53,319 --> 00:15:55,015
It's been powering the GCPD.

354
00:15:55,087 --> 00:15:56,419
Right.

355
00:15:56,489 --> 00:15:58,617
We need to make it a bomb again.

356
00:15:58,691 --> 00:16:00,387
You got to be kidding me.

357
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:03,020
Jeremiah knew exactly
where to put his bombs

358
00:16:03,095 --> 00:16:05,257
to topple buildings,
turn Gotham into a maze.

359
00:16:05,331 --> 00:16:06,594
We stopped him.

360
00:16:06,666 --> 00:16:08,635
But if we could use
just part of his plan,

361
00:16:08,701 --> 00:16:10,636
we can trap the army
and slow them down.

362
00:16:10,703 --> 00:16:12,604
By knocking buildings
down like dominos.

363
00:16:12,672 --> 00:16:15,369
But for that to work, we need
to put a bomb in this building.

364
00:16:15,441 --> 00:16:17,740
Ground Zero for the blast.

365
00:16:18,010 --> 00:16:19,535
Wayne Enterprises.

366
00:16:19,612 --> 00:16:21,171
Bruce...

367
00:16:23,082 --> 00:16:24,448
There's no other way.

368
00:16:24,517 --> 00:16:28,010
Okay. How do we get
this thing out of here?

369
00:16:28,087 --> 00:16:30,127
To use it as a bomb, you
don't need the whole thing.

370
00:16:30,156 --> 00:16:33,684
All you need is... the core...

371
00:16:35,428 --> 00:16:37,158
and the activator.

372
00:16:37,230 --> 00:16:39,165
(electricity powering down)

373
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,161
That's it?

374
00:16:42,235 --> 00:16:43,464
It may look modest,

375
00:16:43,536 --> 00:16:45,164
but all it took was one of these

376
00:16:45,238 --> 00:16:46,433
to blow up an entire bridge.

377
00:16:46,506 --> 00:16:48,099
Not to mention the
Gotham Clock Tower.

378
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:50,006
Bruce, you can't do this alone.

379
00:16:50,076 --> 00:16:51,374
He's not alone.

380
00:16:51,444 --> 00:16:53,310
I know where to place the bomb.

381
00:16:53,379 --> 00:16:55,245
And you and Lucius
are needed here.

382
00:17:03,589 --> 00:17:05,490
I can't believe we're
letting them do this.

383
00:17:05,558 --> 00:17:06,558
Add that to the list

384
00:17:06,626 --> 00:17:09,596
of things that I cannot
believe are happening.

385
00:17:19,272 --> 00:17:20,296
Hey.

386
00:17:20,373 --> 00:17:21,807
What?

387
00:17:22,642 --> 00:17:24,543
(grunting)

388
00:17:24,610 --> 00:17:25,669
(snap)

389
00:17:29,348 --> 00:17:31,044
BARBARA: The key's there.

390
00:17:35,755 --> 00:17:37,621
Where is she? Is she okay?

391
00:17:37,690 --> 00:17:38,800
Yeah, she's
upstairs in the office

392
00:17:38,824 --> 00:17:41,225
with Nyssa and the general.

393
00:17:41,294 --> 00:17:43,505
Nyssa is not gonna stop until
she's killed everyone in Gotham.

394
00:17:43,529 --> 00:17:46,465
One thing at a time,
let's go save our baby.

395
00:17:46,532 --> 00:17:49,058
NYSSA: Hello, Captain Gordon.

396
00:17:50,136 --> 00:17:51,570
(guns cocking)

397
00:17:52,438 --> 00:17:53,770
Ah.

398
00:17:53,839 --> 00:17:57,640
You're seeing your
baby for the first time.

399
00:17:57,710 --> 00:17:59,076
(sighs)

400
00:17:59,145 --> 00:18:01,239
I wish I had a camera.

401
00:18:01,314 --> 00:18:02,314
Hand her over.

402
00:18:02,381 --> 00:18:03,381
No.

403
00:18:03,416 --> 00:18:06,545
I don't think I will.

404
00:18:06,619 --> 00:18:08,554
Put down your guns.

405
00:18:08,621 --> 00:18:12,786
Unless you want the little
one hurt in the crossfire.

406
00:18:14,393 --> 00:18:15,486
(chuckles)

407
00:18:18,598 --> 00:18:21,693
Even now, the army is making
its way to the Green Zone

408
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:24,703
while Bane is hunting
down Bruce Wayne.

409
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:26,636
Only question is,

410
00:18:26,706 --> 00:18:29,107
what to do with you?

411
00:18:34,313 --> 00:18:36,475
This is it.

412
00:18:36,549 --> 00:18:38,177
The bomb will weaken
the support column

413
00:18:38,250 --> 00:18:40,446
and topple the entire building.

414
00:18:40,519 --> 00:18:42,215
This is crazy.

415
00:18:42,288 --> 00:18:45,258
I mean, we've spent this entire
time trying to stop Jeremiah

416
00:18:45,324 --> 00:18:47,190
and now we're actually
using part of his plan.

417
00:18:48,561 --> 00:18:51,121
Believe me...

418
00:18:51,197 --> 00:18:53,462
if there was any other way...

419
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:56,493
SELINA: You sure
you want to do this?

420
00:18:57,336 --> 00:18:59,703
First Wayne Manor gets destroyed

421
00:18:59,772 --> 00:19:02,139
and now Wayne Enterprises.

422
00:19:02,208 --> 00:19:04,871
This building is the heart
of my family's company.

423
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:06,544
There are things above us

424
00:19:06,612 --> 00:19:10,515
my parents spent
their entire lives on.

425
00:19:10,583 --> 00:19:12,449
Some of my earliest memories

426
00:19:12,518 --> 00:19:14,180
are playing with
Alfred in this lobby,

427
00:19:14,253 --> 00:19:16,381
waiting for my parents to
come down these escalators.

428
00:19:17,423 --> 00:19:18,857
But my parents
built this company

429
00:19:18,924 --> 00:19:21,257
to make Gotham a better place.

430
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:26,724
They would have sacrificed
everything for this city.

431
00:19:26,799 --> 00:19:29,769
They did sacrifice everything.

432
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:36,636
And if that's what it takes...

433
00:19:40,513 --> 00:19:42,778
so will I.

434
00:19:43,816 --> 00:19:45,751
(exhales)

435
00:19:45,818 --> 00:19:48,219
SELINA: So remind
me how this works.

436
00:19:48,754 --> 00:19:50,780
Pulls energy from
the air and magnifies it.

437
00:19:52,892 --> 00:19:54,690
And when it does that?

438
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:56,388
We run!

439
00:20:17,249 --> 00:20:19,309
(clamoring)

440
00:20:21,420 --> 00:20:23,651
(screaming)

441
00:20:26,926 --> 00:20:28,861
♪♪♪♪

442
00:20:37,870 --> 00:20:40,669
I knew you'd
come for your child.

443
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:42,709
I just didn't think
you'd be foolish enough

444
00:20:42,775 --> 00:20:44,471
to come alone.

445
00:20:44,543 --> 00:20:46,273
I don't need help
to take you down.

446
00:20:47,279 --> 00:20:48,838
Don't you see?

447
00:20:48,914 --> 00:20:50,780
It's over.

448
00:20:50,850 --> 00:20:52,478
Gotham will burn.

449
00:20:52,551 --> 00:20:55,453
And I'll achieve what
my father couldn't.

450
00:20:55,521 --> 00:20:58,286
Including killing you.

451
00:20:58,357 --> 00:20:59,916
(chuckles)

452
00:20:59,992 --> 00:21:02,587
She likes to be held upright.

453
00:21:02,661 --> 00:21:04,562
(baby cooing) There.

454
00:21:05,731 --> 00:21:09,361
Barbara, I'll deal with you once
Gotham has been destroyed.

455
00:21:10,369 --> 00:21:12,634
But I'd like you to see this.

456
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:16,298
(both grunting)

457
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:30,512
I was expecting
a little more gusto.

458
00:21:30,589 --> 00:21:32,285
You want gusto?

459
00:21:33,292 --> 00:21:35,693
(both grunt)

460
00:21:37,496 --> 00:21:38,896
Is that all you got?
(radio beeping)

461
00:21:40,366 --> 00:21:42,926
It's Lieutenant Angel.

462
00:21:46,438 --> 00:21:47,531
They did what?

463
00:21:47,606 --> 00:21:49,472
No, no.

464
00:21:49,542 --> 00:21:51,568
Is there another way around?

465
00:21:51,644 --> 00:21:53,545
Then tell the army

466
00:21:53,612 --> 00:21:54,978
to blast through.

467
00:21:55,047 --> 00:21:56,845
GORDON: Hey.

468
00:21:56,916 --> 00:21:59,351
I'm not done with you yet.

469
00:21:59,418 --> 00:22:01,717
Your friends may have
bought you some time,

470
00:22:01,787 --> 00:22:04,518
but the Green Zone's
destruction is only delayed.

471
00:22:06,025 --> 00:22:07,653
And now to meet your fate.

472
00:22:07,726 --> 00:22:09,752
(handcuffs close)
Let's meet it together.

473
00:22:11,030 --> 00:22:12,521
(grunting)

474
00:22:12,598 --> 00:22:13,598
Barbara!

475
00:22:13,666 --> 00:22:14,895
(Gordon screams)

476
00:22:16,902 --> 00:22:17,699
(gunfire)

477
00:22:17,770 --> 00:22:18,770
Shoot him.

478
00:22:19,405 --> 00:22:20,532
No.

479
00:22:20,606 --> 00:22:23,405
(grunting)

480
00:22:28,881 --> 00:22:30,645
You think you can defeat me?

481
00:22:30,716 --> 00:22:33,117
Better men and women
have tried and failed.

482
00:22:33,385 --> 00:22:35,013
(grunting)

483
00:22:37,456 --> 00:22:38,651
(shouts)

484
00:22:42,361 --> 00:22:43,659
I'm an al Ghul.

485
00:22:43,729 --> 00:22:46,961
You'll never beat me; I have
my father's blood in my veins.

486
00:22:47,032 --> 00:22:48,864
I am his one true heir.

487
00:22:48,934 --> 00:22:50,698
Do you ever stop talking?

488
00:22:53,806 --> 00:22:54,806
(cries out)

489
00:22:54,874 --> 00:22:57,366
You two do share one thing.

490
00:22:59,044 --> 00:23:02,412
You both love getting
stabbed by this knife.

491
00:23:02,481 --> 00:23:03,915
General Wade.

492
00:23:05,818 --> 00:23:08,583
Execute fail-safe.

493
00:23:11,957 --> 00:23:13,391
No.

494
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:24,860
I'm going to enjoy watching
Gotham be destroyed!

495
00:23:24,937 --> 00:23:27,839
And then my legacy
will be complete.

496
00:23:37,683 --> 00:23:38,946
We got to hurry.

497
00:23:39,018 --> 00:23:41,129
It's only a matter of time
before the army breaks through.

498
00:23:41,153 --> 00:23:42,553
We need to get back to the GCPD.

499
00:23:42,621 --> 00:23:44,487
- (grunts)
- Bruce!

500
00:23:45,591 --> 00:23:47,958
Impressive. You blew
up your father's building

501
00:23:48,027 --> 00:23:49,655
to stop the military.

502
00:23:49,728 --> 00:23:50,957
It will take more to stop me.

503
00:23:51,030 --> 00:23:52,030
Go on ahead, Selina!

504
00:23:52,097 --> 00:23:53,156
Warn the GCPD!

505
00:23:53,432 --> 00:23:55,458
No, we're doing this together.

506
00:24:17,523 --> 00:24:19,082
You shouldn't have hurt Alfred.

507
00:24:19,158 --> 00:24:22,890
Collateral damage.
It happens in war.

508
00:24:27,132 --> 00:24:30,762
I'm sorry you weren't there
to see me break your butler,

509
00:24:30,836 --> 00:24:33,533
but I'm so glad you won't
miss me killing your little friend.

510
00:24:33,605 --> 00:24:35,597
Let her go.

511
00:24:35,674 --> 00:24:37,905
In war, there are
no attachments.

512
00:24:37,977 --> 00:24:39,912
Only then can you fight
without your hands tied.

513
00:24:39,979 --> 00:24:44,178
You see... just a little
ounce of pressure.

514
00:24:44,249 --> 00:24:46,616
That's all that separates
the living from the dead.

515
00:24:46,685 --> 00:24:48,517
(shouts) (cries out)

516
00:24:51,557 --> 00:24:54,026
(device beeping)

517
00:24:54,093 --> 00:24:55,493
SELINA: What is that?

518
00:24:55,561 --> 00:24:57,138
BRUCE: Wayne cloaking
device, but it had some glitches.

519
00:24:57,162 --> 00:24:59,791
Apparently, it's a beacon
for certain winged mammals.

520
00:24:59,865 --> 00:25:01,060
SELINA: What winged mammals?

521
00:25:01,133 --> 00:25:02,567
(wings flapping)

522
00:25:02,634 --> 00:25:04,569
(squealing)

523
00:25:06,138 --> 00:25:07,697
Bats.

524
00:25:10,976 --> 00:25:12,911
(pained grunting)

525
00:25:39,571 --> 00:25:41,540
There's no way to
reverse the invasion order.

526
00:25:41,607 --> 00:25:43,269
We have to find another way.

527
00:25:43,542 --> 00:25:45,636
- Is she all right?
- She is now.

528
00:25:45,711 --> 00:25:48,579
There, there. Mama's
here. (baby cooing)

529
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:55,084
And your father.

530
00:25:58,857 --> 00:26:00,291
Try not to get blood on her.

531
00:26:24,750 --> 00:26:26,651
Sir...
- (rasping): Come on.

532
00:26:26,718 --> 00:26:28,687
We're almost at the Green Zone.

533
00:26:28,754 --> 00:26:31,019
(mask whirring and clicking)

534
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:33,889
(hisses)

535
00:26:33,959 --> 00:26:36,121
(breathing steadily)

536
00:26:38,931 --> 00:26:39,931
Lee?

537
00:26:41,233 --> 00:26:42,724
Jim.

538
00:26:42,801 --> 00:26:44,702
The baby? I checked
her over, she's fine.

539
00:26:44,770 --> 00:26:45,999
Though she could use a feed.

540
00:26:46,071 --> 00:26:48,267
(baby cooing)

541
00:26:48,340 --> 00:26:50,639
Where's General Wade?
The army's broken through.

542
00:26:50,709 --> 00:26:52,143
General Wade's dead.

543
00:26:52,211 --> 00:26:54,146
Nyssa al Ghul
escaped. There's no way

544
00:26:54,213 --> 00:26:55,704
to order the army to stand down.

545
00:26:55,781 --> 00:26:57,340
So, now what?

546
00:26:57,616 --> 00:27:00,085
The army blew up
Wayne Enterprises

547
00:27:00,152 --> 00:27:02,781
and knocked down
two other buildings.

548
00:27:02,855 --> 00:27:04,323
We don't stand a chance.

549
00:27:04,389 --> 00:27:06,187
Actually, that was
Bruce and Selina.

550
00:27:06,258 --> 00:27:07,783
What?

551
00:27:07,860 --> 00:27:09,226
The army's blocks away.

552
00:27:09,294 --> 00:27:11,160
GORDON: From what
direction? Every direction.

553
00:27:11,230 --> 00:27:12,230
We're surrounded.

554
00:27:13,265 --> 00:27:16,167
Jim. I need to get
her out of here.

555
00:27:16,235 --> 00:27:19,797
All right. The tunnels
underneath the GCPD.

556
00:27:19,872 --> 00:27:22,637
There's a vent shaft, it
connects to the subway line.

557
00:27:22,708 --> 00:27:26,145
Take the baby and the
refugees down into the subways.

558
00:27:26,211 --> 00:27:27,839
Get 'em behind enemy lines.

559
00:27:27,913 --> 00:27:29,779
- Don't stop till
you get to safety.
- Okay.

560
00:27:29,848 --> 00:27:31,817
But what about you?

561
00:27:33,318 --> 00:27:36,345
We'll hold 'em off outside,
buy you some time.

562
00:27:36,421 --> 00:27:37,821
- Jim...
- These refugees,

563
00:27:37,890 --> 00:27:39,100
most of them are
from the Narrows.

564
00:27:39,124 --> 00:27:40,387
They know you, they trust you.

565
00:27:40,659 --> 00:27:42,321
They know you'll protect them.

566
00:27:44,062 --> 00:27:45,655
Go.

567
00:27:54,706 --> 00:27:57,938
Oh, there you are, Master Bruce.

568
00:27:58,010 --> 00:28:00,036
Rest, Alfred.

569
00:28:01,146 --> 00:28:04,139
All this time, I
tried to protect you.

570
00:28:04,216 --> 00:28:07,243
Here you are, a soldier.

571
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:10,947
A soldier for good.

572
00:28:11,023 --> 00:28:13,925
You've spent your
life protecting me.

573
00:28:14,426 --> 00:28:17,021
Now it's time for
me to do the same.

574
00:28:17,095 --> 00:28:19,860
It's time for me
to protect Gotham.

575
00:28:20,465 --> 00:28:22,297
Even if there's
nothing left to defend.

576
00:28:32,978 --> 00:28:34,947
All right, everyone,
let's move. Okay.

577
00:28:35,013 --> 00:28:37,346
All right, you'll walk about
five blocks underground,

578
00:28:37,416 --> 00:28:40,386
and then you'll get
to a subway vent. Go.

579
00:28:43,255 --> 00:28:45,247
You're not coming with us?

580
00:28:45,324 --> 00:28:47,759
Jim and our friends are
out there making a stand.

581
00:28:47,826 --> 00:28:48,850
That's where I belong.

582
00:28:48,927 --> 00:28:50,471
Wait, what are we
going to do without you?

583
00:28:50,495 --> 00:28:55,024
Survive. Make sure
this was all worth it. Go.

584
00:29:01,940 --> 00:29:03,238
What was that for?

585
00:29:03,308 --> 00:29:05,004
Everything you've done for me.

586
00:29:05,077 --> 00:29:06,875
And for her.

587
00:29:06,945 --> 00:29:08,914
Just get them to safety.

588
00:29:34,906 --> 00:29:37,102
It's over, Jim.

589
00:29:37,175 --> 00:29:39,872
Our war's come to an end.

590
00:29:39,945 --> 00:29:44,110
This isn't a war.
This is a firing squad.

591
00:29:47,919 --> 00:29:48,943
I told you to go.

592
00:29:49,021 --> 00:29:50,216
And I didn't listen.

593
00:29:50,289 --> 00:29:51,780
Ready.

594
00:29:51,857 --> 00:29:52,857
(panting)

595
00:29:52,924 --> 00:29:55,416
Aim.

596
00:29:55,494 --> 00:29:57,429
(rifles cocking)

597
00:30:00,098 --> 00:30:02,260
MAN: Shoulder to shoulder.

598
00:30:02,334 --> 00:30:03,962
- Stand together.
- What the...?

599
00:30:09,074 --> 00:30:10,838
They're here for us, Jim.

600
00:30:21,186 --> 00:30:22,848
Fire.

601
00:30:22,921 --> 00:30:24,514
(crowd quiets)

602
00:30:27,025 --> 00:30:29,392
I said fire!

603
00:30:29,461 --> 00:30:31,020
GORDON: You have a choice.

604
00:30:31,530 --> 00:30:35,592
You can stand with us, or
you can stand with them.

605
00:30:55,053 --> 00:30:57,852
(crowd cheering)

606
00:31:11,002 --> 00:31:13,597
CROWD (chanting): We are Gotham!

607
00:31:13,872 --> 00:31:16,865
We are Gotham! We are Gotham!

608
00:31:20,912 --> 00:31:22,972
(coughing)

609
00:31:29,354 --> 00:31:33,485
So that bitch was
telling the truth after all.

610
00:31:38,096 --> 00:31:40,031
(dog barking)

611
00:31:50,642 --> 00:31:52,487
LUCIUS: We managed to
raise the mainland on the radio.

612
00:31:52,511 --> 00:31:54,104
They know everything.
As of right now,

613
00:31:54,179 --> 00:31:55,647
the army's being repurposed

614
00:31:55,914 --> 00:31:58,076
for the humanitarian
mission of rebuilding Gotham.

615
00:31:58,150 --> 00:32:01,245
These refugees will get
food, water, medical treatment.

616
00:32:01,319 --> 00:32:03,515
They're setting up a crisis
center in Federal Square.

617
00:32:03,588 --> 00:32:05,489
I'll be damned.

618
00:32:05,557 --> 00:32:07,458
Hey.

619
00:32:10,095 --> 00:32:11,529
So...

620
00:32:12,197 --> 00:32:13,688
this whole "not
listening" thing.

621
00:32:13,965 --> 00:32:15,456
It's not gonna
become a habit, is it?

622
00:32:16,435 --> 00:32:17,994
You're welcome.

623
00:32:25,977 --> 00:32:27,104
Go.

624
00:32:34,453 --> 00:32:36,115
(chuckles softly)

625
00:32:36,188 --> 00:32:37,281
Well, this is gonna make

626
00:32:37,355 --> 00:32:40,416
one hell of a bedtime
story some day.

627
00:32:41,460 --> 00:32:43,156
Can I?

628
00:32:43,228 --> 00:32:45,424
Of course.

629
00:32:50,335 --> 00:32:53,066
I don't even know
what to call her.

630
00:32:53,138 --> 00:32:54,731
Barbara.

631
00:32:56,641 --> 00:32:57,641
Oh.

632
00:32:58,443 --> 00:33:00,969
Barbara Lee Gordon.

633
00:33:01,046 --> 00:33:04,574
In this city, it's important
she know who she can rely on.

634
00:33:04,649 --> 00:33:06,709
(cooing)

635
00:33:20,599 --> 00:33:22,329
Bruce, what's wrong?

636
00:33:27,439 --> 00:33:29,032
We won.

637
00:33:29,107 --> 00:33:31,633
Nyssa al Ghul
is still out there.

638
00:33:31,710 --> 00:33:34,771
And she and Bane were right.

639
00:33:35,046 --> 00:33:37,379
All this happened because of me,

640
00:33:37,449 --> 00:33:39,350
because people
were trying to hurt me

641
00:33:39,417 --> 00:33:41,545
and the people I care about.

642
00:33:42,587 --> 00:33:44,715
When Bane had you...

643
00:33:47,192 --> 00:33:48,569
I thought he was
gonna kill you, Selina,

644
00:33:48,593 --> 00:33:50,562
and there was
nothing I could do.

645
00:33:51,162 --> 00:33:53,028
Hey.

646
00:33:53,098 --> 00:33:54,794
I will be here

647
00:33:55,066 --> 00:33:56,762
whenever you need me.

648
00:34:00,138 --> 00:34:01,538
What?

649
00:34:02,574 --> 00:34:05,476
That's what my
parents used to tell me.

650
00:34:07,212 --> 00:34:08,612
Come here.

651
00:34:16,054 --> 00:34:18,250
That bitch stole our submarine!

652
00:34:18,323 --> 00:34:19,382
And our gold.

653
00:34:19,457 --> 00:34:21,221
And by now she's probably landed

654
00:34:21,293 --> 00:34:23,762
somewhere on the
mainland, impossible to track!

655
00:34:23,828 --> 00:34:26,093
After all we've been
through these last months,

656
00:34:26,164 --> 00:34:28,395
we are once again
left with nothing!

657
00:34:28,466 --> 00:34:29,729
Nothing!

658
00:34:29,801 --> 00:34:30,801
(grunts)

659
00:34:31,069 --> 00:34:33,538
Back to square one.

660
00:34:33,605 --> 00:34:35,096
Common criminals.

661
00:34:35,173 --> 00:34:37,665
We saved this city
from certain damnation,

662
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:40,234
but will we see any
credit for our loyalty,

663
00:34:40,312 --> 00:34:41,712
our selfless bravery?

664
00:34:41,780 --> 00:34:43,078
Of course not!

665
00:34:43,148 --> 00:34:44,514
I don't want their thanks.

666
00:34:44,583 --> 00:34:46,711
(panting)

667
00:34:46,785 --> 00:34:48,754
Or their respect.

668
00:34:49,754 --> 00:34:51,518
You know what I felt,

669
00:34:51,590 --> 00:34:55,152
standing shoulder to shoulder
with those people out there?

670
00:34:59,230 --> 00:35:00,721
Nothing.

671
00:35:02,734 --> 00:35:04,396
I...

672
00:35:04,469 --> 00:35:06,233
feel...

673
00:35:06,871 --> 00:35:09,670
absolutely nothing

674
00:35:09,741 --> 00:35:12,609
for those drab...

675
00:35:13,511 --> 00:35:15,309
boring people.

676
00:35:15,780 --> 00:35:17,806
That was me once.

677
00:35:18,483 --> 00:35:21,351
Minimum wage at a thankless job

678
00:35:21,419 --> 00:35:22,614
at the GCPD.

679
00:35:22,687 --> 00:35:23,746
"Yes, sir. No, sir.

680
00:35:23,822 --> 00:35:26,121
Thank you so much, sir."

681
00:35:26,591 --> 00:35:29,390
Picking up scraps
from my master's floor.

682
00:35:29,461 --> 00:35:32,192
Shy, awkward...

683
00:35:32,263 --> 00:35:34,892
pathetic Ed.

684
00:35:42,273 --> 00:35:44,208
Common criminals?

685
00:35:45,710 --> 00:35:47,679
Never again.

686
00:35:48,413 --> 00:35:51,906
I've shown this city who
I truly am once before,

687
00:35:52,183 --> 00:35:54,243
and I will do it again.

688
00:35:54,319 --> 00:35:56,788
They will bow

689
00:35:56,855 --> 00:35:59,290
to the Riddler, and
they won't get up

690
00:35:59,357 --> 00:36:02,919
until I permit them to.

691
00:36:03,194 --> 00:36:04,890
Yes.

692
00:36:05,163 --> 00:36:06,893
You're right.

693
00:36:07,165 --> 00:36:09,327
Our accomplishments
have been erased,

694
00:36:09,401 --> 00:36:12,394
our brilliant minds underrated.

695
00:36:12,470 --> 00:36:15,269
If they had let me run this
city the way I wanted to,

696
00:36:15,340 --> 00:36:17,536
it would not be in ruins now.

697
00:36:17,609 --> 00:36:19,635
I have the men, the money,

698
00:36:19,711 --> 00:36:22,510
- the guns...
- Gordon took them.

699
00:36:22,580 --> 00:36:24,481
Why? Because he still sees you

700
00:36:24,549 --> 00:36:27,178
as Fish Mooney's umbrella
boy, and he always will.

701
00:36:27,552 --> 00:36:28,576
Yes.

702
00:36:29,387 --> 00:36:31,253
I only came back to
help him save this city

703
00:36:31,322 --> 00:36:34,224
so that I could
take it for myself.

704
00:36:34,292 --> 00:36:36,227
We would be stronger together.

705
00:36:37,796 --> 00:36:39,526
No one could stop us.

706
00:36:40,265 --> 00:36:42,234
Yeah, perhaps.

707
00:36:49,407 --> 00:36:50,966
Let's make a pact,

708
00:36:51,242 --> 00:36:53,404
here and now.

709
00:36:53,478 --> 00:36:55,606
We will take what we want

710
00:36:55,680 --> 00:36:57,649
from who we want,

711
00:36:57,716 --> 00:37:00,618
and we will suffer no fools.

712
00:37:02,520 --> 00:37:04,352
Together.

713
00:37:05,423 --> 00:37:07,221
Shall we shake on that?

714
00:37:08,226 --> 00:37:09,592
Please,

715
00:37:09,661 --> 00:37:11,789
we're brothers.

716
00:37:11,863 --> 00:37:13,832
A hug.

717
00:37:14,966 --> 00:37:16,559
A hug it is.

718
00:37:16,634 --> 00:37:18,865
(panting)

719
00:37:32,517 --> 00:37:33,985
(sighs)

720
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:44,286
Life begins anew.

721
00:37:47,866 --> 00:37:49,892
Shall we get to work?

722
00:37:57,675 --> 00:37:59,507
MAN: <i>Thank you all
for coming here today.</i>

723
00:37:59,577 --> 00:38:02,945
<i>It is my great honor to
introduce Mayor Chang.</i>

724
00:38:03,014 --> 00:38:04,778
(crowd murmuring)

725
00:38:04,849 --> 00:38:07,478
CHANG: <i>With
reunification underway</i>

726
00:38:07,552 --> 00:38:09,851
<i>and the bridges being rebuilt,</i>

727
00:38:09,921 --> 00:38:13,688
<i>it is my honor to bestow
upon Captain James Gordon</i>

728
00:38:13,758 --> 00:38:16,353
<i>the title of commissioner.</i>

729
00:38:16,427 --> 00:38:18,362
(applause)

730
00:38:31,810 --> 00:38:34,507
(indistinct chatter)

731
00:38:34,579 --> 00:38:36,844
We're gonna miss
you around the bullpen.

732
00:38:36,915 --> 00:38:38,884
I won't be far.

733
00:38:38,950 --> 00:38:40,748
And the mission doesn't change.

734
00:38:41,386 --> 00:38:44,015
Still trying to make
this city a better place.

735
00:38:44,088 --> 00:38:45,556
Be careful.

736
00:38:45,623 --> 00:38:47,091
You're swimming with sharks now.

737
00:38:52,430 --> 00:38:54,592
If you need anything, ever...

738
00:38:54,666 --> 00:38:56,635
I know who to call.

739
00:39:01,973 --> 00:39:04,602
You deserve this, Jim.

740
00:39:04,676 --> 00:39:06,804
You really do.

741
00:39:07,612 --> 00:39:09,740
I'm gonna go get
a drink before...

742
00:39:09,814 --> 00:39:11,510
you get all teary-eyed on me.

743
00:39:11,583 --> 00:39:13,518
(sniffles)

744
00:39:19,891 --> 00:39:21,382
What do you mean,
you're leaving?

745
00:39:21,459 --> 00:39:23,052
Bane's in prison, it's over.

746
00:39:23,728 --> 00:39:28,132
My life here... it's too public.

747
00:39:29,067 --> 00:39:30,592
You've made up your mind.

748
00:39:30,668 --> 00:39:32,068
Gotham's in good hands.

749
00:39:33,471 --> 00:39:34,495
Commissioner.

750
00:39:34,572 --> 00:39:36,097
Yeah.

751
00:39:39,377 --> 00:39:40,970
Thank you, Bruce,

752
00:39:41,045 --> 00:39:44,038
for everything you've
done for me and for the city.

753
00:39:45,583 --> 00:39:47,711
Gotham will always be your home.

754
00:40:00,765 --> 00:40:02,529
Bruce is all grown up.

755
00:40:03,501 --> 00:40:04,799
- That he is.
- Well,

756
00:40:04,869 --> 00:40:06,861
now you have another
little one to look after.

757
00:40:16,915 --> 00:40:18,747
Where's Bruce?

758
00:40:18,816 --> 00:40:20,876
Um...

759
00:40:21,719 --> 00:40:23,585
he left you this.

760
00:40:34,866 --> 00:40:36,801
(shuddering)

761
00:40:54,452 --> 00:40:57,718
BRUCE: You know how to
reach me if you need anything?

762
00:40:58,756 --> 00:41:00,190
Yes.

763
00:41:01,526 --> 00:41:05,463
Well, you know me, Master
Bruce, I'll be very self-sufficient.

764
00:41:07,098 --> 00:41:10,500
Busy, actually. You know,
we start the reconstruction

765
00:41:10,568 --> 00:41:13,732
of Wayne Enterprises and
Wayne Manor tomorrow.

766
00:41:15,673 --> 00:41:18,507
You will remember everything
I taught you, won't you?

767
00:41:20,011 --> 00:41:21,479
Of course.

768
00:41:25,216 --> 00:41:28,914
Good, that's... that's good.

769
00:41:30,088 --> 00:41:32,956
I never tried to replace
your parents, you know?

770
00:41:34,692 --> 00:41:36,684
I couldn't, I never would.

771
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:40,791
But I want you to
know, Master Bruce,

772
00:41:40,865 --> 00:41:42,128
that you are the only son

773
00:41:42,200 --> 00:41:44,635
that I will ever have,

774
00:41:44,702 --> 00:41:46,898
and I could not be more proud.

775
00:41:55,079 --> 00:41:56,570
(shuddering)

776
00:42:25,877 --> 00:42:27,812
(turbine whirring)

777
00:42:37,989 --> 00:42:39,924
(airplane taking off)

778
00:43:01,646 --> 00:43:03,581
♪♪♪♪
